# Graphics and tilesets

- **`graphics/`**: Source art (tiles, sprites, UI). Naming and folder layout should match similar assets; follow existing bit depth and dimensions for the asset class (sprites vs backgrounds vs UI).
- **`data/tilesets/`**: Built or authored tileset data (metatiles, palettes). Palette indices and transparency rules must stay consistent with how maps reference the tileset.
- **`graphics_file_rules.mk`**: Declares how graphics convert into objects the build consumes. When adding a new graphic, copy the pattern of the closest existing rule (same tool chain, same output type).

Prefer **regenerating** from source assets over hand-editing compiled binary blobs when the repo already uses a tool for that path.
